---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CalculatorPage from '../components/CalculatorPage.astro';

const title = 'Student Loan Planning & College Financial Aid Tools';
const description = 'Free student loan planning and college financial aid tools: compare federal repayment plans, estimate RAP payments, and compare college aid offers without an account.';
---
<Base {title} {description} kind="WebApplication">
  <header class="decision-hero page-hero">
    <div class="decision-intro">
      <span class="decision-eyebrow page-hero-kicker">Your student loan planning workspace</span>
      <h1>Student loan and college aid tools</h1>
      <p>Know your options. Understand the numbers. Compare loan payments, understand total repayment costs, and check the real price of college with free, independent tools.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="primary button-link" href="#repayment-estimator">Estimate loan payments</a>
        <a class="secondary button-link" href="/tools/compare-college-aid-offers/">Compare aid offers</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">No account required · Runs in your browser · Estimates for planning</p>
    </div>
    <section class="decision-options" aria-label="Choose a starting point">
      <h2 class="decision-options-heading">What do you need help with?</h2>
      <a class="decision-option" href="/tools/compare-college-aid-offers/">
        <span class="decision-option-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div><strong>Choosing a college?</strong><span>Compare the real cost of two schools after grants, scholarships, and planned loans.</span></div>
        <span class="decision-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="decision-option" href="/deadlines/">
        <span class="decision-option-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div><strong>Already repaying loans?</strong><span>Explore repayment timelines and the questions to check with your loan servicer.</span></div>
        <span class="decision-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="decision-option" href="/guides/compare-student-loan-repayment/">
        <span class="decision-option-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div><strong>Not sure what to compare?</strong><span>Learn why a lower payment can still lead to a higher overall cost.</span></div>
        <span class="decision-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </section>
  </header>

  <section class="home-goal-banner page-section" aria-labelledby="home-goal-title">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Not sure where to begin?</span>
      <h2 id="home-goal-title">Not sure which tool fits? Start here.</h2>
      <p>Choose your situation and get a clear next step—no technical loan terms required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="home-goal-actions">
      <a class="primary button-link" href="/tools/#find-a-tool">Find my tool</a>
      <a class="secondary button-link" href="/guides/#find-my-guide">Find an explanation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CalculatorPage title="Student loan repayment calculator" embedded />

  <section class="home-explain page-section" aria-labelledby="understand-results">
    <div class="home-section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Understand your estimate</span>
      <h2 id="understand-results">Three numbers worth understanding.</h2>
      <p>Compare the same loan information across options. LoanLens helps organize the numbers, while official sources and your servicer confirm which choices are available to you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="home-cards">
      <article class="home-info-card">
        <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h3>Monthly payment</h3>
        <p>Check the estimated amount due each month and whether a changing income could affect future payments.</p>
        <a href="/calculator/">Federal student loan repayment calculator</a>
      </article>
      <article class="home-info-card">
        <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h3>Overall repayment cost</h3>
        <p>Look beyond the first payment to the amount paid across the projection, including the effect of time and interest.</p>
        <a href="/guides/compare-student-loan-repayment/">Learn how to compare costs</a>
      </article>
      <article class="home-info-card">
        <span class="card-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h3>College net price</h3>
        <p>Subtract grants and scholarships from the annual cost of attendance, then see how planned borrowing changes the remaining gap.</p>
        <a href="/tools/compare-college-aid-offers/">Compare two college offers</a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="home-note">
      <div>
        <strong>Built for clearer decisions, not official eligibility checks.</strong>
        <p>Your figures are modeled estimates. LoanLens cannot access your student loan account, confirm repayment eligibility, or enroll you in a plan. Cross-check repayment choices with <a href="https://studentaid.gov/loan-simulator/">Federal Student Aid's official calculator</a> and your loan servicer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-questions page-section" aria-labelledby="common-questions">
    <div class="home-section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Quick answers</span>
      <h2 id="common-questions">Questions worth asking before you choose.</h2>
      <p>Understand the limits of the estimate and follow a useful next step. No sales pressure, just practical context.</p>
      <div class="page-intro-links">
        <a href="/rap-payment-by-income/">RAP payment calculator by income</a>
        <a href="/guides/rap-vs-ibr/">Compare RAP vs. IBR</a>
        <a href="/guides/">Read repayment guides</a>
        <a href="/tools/">Browse all tools</a>
        <a href="/guides/faq/">Student loan FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="home-question-list">
      <details>
        <summary>Can this calculator see my student loan account?</summary>
        <p>No. Enter a loan balance and rate yourself. The calculator processes your scenario in your browser; it does not sign in to Federal Student Aid or contact your servicer. Be careful with shared scenario links, which contain the values you entered. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the lowest monthly payment always the cheapest plan?</summary>
        <p>Not necessarily. A smaller payment over a longer period can add up to more paid overall. Compare the estimated monthly amount, number of months, total paid, and any forgiveness assumptions using the <a href="/guides/compare-student-loan-repayment/">repayment comparison guide</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What's the difference between net price and the amount left after loans?</summary>
        <p>Net price is a college's annual cost after grants and scholarships. Loans may reduce the amount you need to cover immediately, but they remain money you must repay. Use the <a href="/guides/compare-college-financial-aid-offers/">financial aid comparison guide</a> for an example.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I apply for a repayment plan on LoanLens?</summary>
        <p>No. LoanLens is an independent educational resource. Verify eligibility and complete any repayment application through <a href="https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/repayment/plans">Federal Student Aid</a> or your loan servicer.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
